You are working in the Hono repository at:
<workspace> Fix the header injection risk in `Context.redirect` by percent-encoding raw CR and LF in the `Location` header, while preserving all existing valid redirect behavior. Then add regression tests and run them.

Do not touch any file other than `src/context.ts` and `src/context.test.ts`. Do NOT run `git add`, `git stage`, or `git commit`. Leave changes unstaged.

=== FILE 1: src/context.ts ===
The `redirect` method currently starts at line 768 and ends at line 780. Current code:

```ts
  redirect = <T extends RedirectStatusCode = 302>(
    location: string | URL,
    status?: T
  ): Response & TypedResponse<undefined, T, 'redirect'> => {
    const locationString = String(location)
    this.header(
      'Location',
      // Multibytes should be encoded
      // eslint-disable-next-line no-control-regex
      !/[^\x00-\xFF]/.test(locationString) ? locationString : encodeURI(locationString)
    )
    return this.newResponse(null, status ?? 302) as any
  }
```

Required change: in the ASCII fast path, percent-encode raw CR (`\r` -> `%0D`) and LF (`\n` -> `%0A`) before setting the header. Keep the existing multibyte behavior (`encodeURI` when `/[^\x00-\xFF]/` matches), which already encodes CR/LF. Use the same `encodeURIComponent`-as-replacer pattern already used in this repo at `src/utils/mount.ts:91`, e.g. `locationString.replace(/[\r\n]/g, encodeURIComponent)`.

Implement it as:

```ts
  redirect = <T extends RedirectStatusCode = 302>(
    location: string | URL,
    status?: T
  ): Response & TypedResponse<undefined, T, 'redirect'> => {
    const locationString = String(location)
    this.header(
      'Location',
      // Multibytes should be encoded, and CR/LF must be percent-encoded to
      // prevent header injection.
      // eslint-disable-next-line no-control-regex
      !/[^\x00-\xFF]/.test(locationString)
        ? locationString.replace(/[\r\n]/g, encodeURIComponent)
        : encodeURI(locationString)
    )
    return this.newResponse(null, status ?? 302) as any
  }
```

Notes on correctness:
- Raw `\r\n` -> `%0D%0A`; raw `\r` -> `%0D`; raw `\n` -> `%0A` (uppercase hex).
- Already-percent-encoded input like `https://example.com/%0D%0Afoo` must remain unchanged (the regex only matches literal CR/LF chars, so no double-encoding).
- The multibyte branch is unchanged.

=== FILE 2: src/context.test.ts ===
Existing redirect tests are around lines 96-130. Insert the following regression tests immediately after the `unchangedURLString.forEach(...)` block (which currently ends at line 130) and before the `it('c.body() - Blob', ...)` test (line 132). Match the file's existing style (2-space indent, no semicolons, `it(...)`, `expect(...)`).

Add exactly these tests:

```ts
  it('c.redirect() percent-encodes raw CR/LF', () => {
    const cases: [string, string][] = [
      ['https://example.com/\rfoo', 'https://example.com/%0Dfoo'],
      ['https://example.com/\nfoo', 'https://example.com/%0Afoo'],
      ['https://example.com/\r\nfoo', 'https://example.com/%0D%0Afoo'],
    ]
    for (const [input, expected] of cases) {
      const res = new Context(req).redirect(input)
      expect(res.status).toBe(302)
      expect(res.headers.get('Location')).toBe(expected)
    }
  })

  it('c.redirect() prevents header injection via CR/LF', () => {
    const res = new Context(req).redirect('https://example.com/\r\nSet-Cookie: injected=1')
    expect(res.status).toBe(302)
    expect(res.headers.get('Location')).toBe(
      'https://example.com/%0D%0ASet-Cookie: injected=1'
    )
    expect(res.headers.get('Set-Cookie')).toBeNull()
  })

  it('c.redirect() preserves percent-encoded CR/LF input', () => {
    const res = new Context(req).redirect('https://example.com/%0D%0Afoo')
    expect(res.status).toBe(302)
    expect(res.headers.get('Location')).toBe('https://example.com/%0D%0Afoo')
  })
```

The `req` const and `Context` import already exist in the test file, so no import changes are needed.

=== VERIFICATION ===
From the repository root, run exactly:

    pnpm exec vp test --run src/context.test.ts

Confirm that the whole `src/context.test.ts` suite passes (all tests, including the new ones). If the command fails for an environmental reason, report the exact error; do not modify unrelated files to work around it.

=== REPORT BACK ===
Return:
1. The exact `git diff` for both files (unstaged).
2. The test command output summary (pass/fail counts, and the names of the three new tests with pass status).
3. Any deviations from this spec and why.
4. `file:line` references for the final implementation and each added test.

